   printf "<b>Highest Seeds Report for All Seasons<p></b>";
   
   #prints as-of-dates for the report.      
   ($today,$max_tmp_date_asdate)=&get_today;
   printf "Data on screen printed ${today}.  Latest tourney in DB is as of ${max_tmp_date_asdate}.<p>";      

   printf "This query shows the highest seeds to win a tourney, make a final, make the quarters, etc for all available data in the database.  
   Keep in mind that seeding data was only reliably captured starting in the 2010-11 season.  There are some tourneys going back in time where 
   we have captured seeding data and those may show up herein.</b> <p>";

   if ($form{'tour'} eq 'IRT') {
      printf "Two of the most 'important' low-seed wins in the history of the tour are two of the only times in recorded history where a 
	  qualifier has won a tournament; Cliff Swain in 1985 Tulsa and Kane Waselenchuk upon his return from suspension in Denver 2008.  
	  I've manually found and re-created the seedings from these two tournaments to make this report show these two results.  
